tools.details:
Each value is a CSS selector, optionally with "@attr" to read an attribute ("a@href", "img@src"; href/src come back absolute). Without @attr you get the text (or a form field's value). A one-item list returns every match, and an object with "_selector" scopes its fields to that element. Example:

{"title": "h1", "products": [{"_selector": ".product", "name": "h3", "price": ".price", "url": "a@href"}], "tags": [".tag"]}

Selectors use the main document (not iframes or shadow DOM).
